{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Then he sang</b> — two times here, and the other: \"Then Israel sang\" (Numbers 21:17). To say: even though the name of Moses is not mentioned there, nevertheless he too said shirah just as here, except they did not mention it because he was stricken through water." "<b>Then he sang</b> — He spoke in the language of complaint: \"And from when I came to Pharaoh\" (Exodus 5:23); in that same language I begin to praise and to extol." "<b>He sang</b> — יו\"ד שיר שיו\"ד שירות הן. ים. באר. האזינו. יהושע. דבורה. חנה. דוד. שלמה. חזקיה. ושירה לעתיד." "<b>I will sing</b> — Three times in the Masorah: here; and the other: \"I — to YHWH, I will sing\" (Judges 5:3), just as here they drowned in the Sea of Reeds, so too there the brook Kishon swept them away; and the other: \"Let me sing now to my beloved, a song of my beloved concerning his vineyard\" (Isaiah 5:1) — on account of: \"A vine from Egypt You did uproot\" (Psalm 80:9)."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The phrase 'אז ישיר' appears twice with this spelling in Scripture — here and at Numbers 21:17. The 'other' (אידך) refers to that second occurrence.", 2 "The phrase 'יו״ד שיר' means 'ten songs'; 'שיו״ד שירות' means 'which are [the number] י״ד = 14 songs including the future one.' The list names nine past songs plus the future song, totaling ten, and the calculation adds four more to reach fourteen — the exact logic of his count is not spelled out."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:01.956939466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}